{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `log_radon`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual per-observation `target += normal_lpdf(...)` likelihood loop with a single built-in vectorized sampling statement, `log_radon ~ normal(mu, sigma_y);`, where `mu` is computed deterministically before the observation is scored. No data fields were added or changed. All parameters retain their original built-in prior sampling statements before they are used in the model likelihood.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> J;
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county_idx;
  vector[N] floor_measure;
  vector[N] log_radon;
}
parameters {
  real alpha;
  vector[J] beta_raw;
  real mu_beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma_beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[J] beta;
  // implies: beta ~ normal(mu_beta, sigma_beta);
  beta = mu_beta + sigma_beta * beta_raw;
}
model {
  vector[N] mu;
  // Prior
  alpha ~ normal(0, 10);
  sigma_y ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_beta ~ normal(0, 1);
  mu_beta ~ normal(0, 10);
  beta_raw ~ normal(0, 1);

  for (n in 1 : N) {
    mu[n] = alpha + floor_measure[n] * beta[county_idx[n]];
  }
  log_radon ~ normal(mu, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":2,"N":4,"county_idx":[2,2,2,2],"floor_measure":[3.1114349971254684,3.6083083343230413,4.624187697444311,3.4498122645788265],"log_radon":[6.463084219400565,2.6963255365853938,5.082355376920726,2.242204635689004]}","protected_variables":["log_radon"]}
